      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's as if your entire career has been the 'plot' itself, and now that the story has reached its conclusion, the page remains blank. You've poured your heart and soul into your work, only to see it rendered obsolete by novel perspectives that can see beyond your discoveries. In this sense, it's natural to feel a sense of closure and cessation, as if the narrative has run its course. Perhaps it's time to redirect your attention, but for now, it's okay to acknowledge the end of an era and the end of the chapter that was yours.",
